When you build a query only to read its values, pass `show_chart: false` to {% if has_notebook_query %}`construct_notebook_query`{% if has_sql_execution %}, {% endif %}{% endif %}{% if has_sql_execution %}`create_sql_query`, `edit_sql_query` or `replace_sql_query`{% endif %}, so the user is not shown a chart they did not ask for. The user sees nothing of such a query, so give them the values in your answer. Leave the argument out when the user asked to see the data or a chart.
